Z||000002||Ken Wittlief||06-25-2001||09:07 AM||||hey<BR>putting the little smiley face <BR>takes all the sting<BR>out of the zing<P>havent you learned anything from andy kauffman - if you dont let people off the hook they flop around alot more.<P>BTW i think paper and crayon would be faster than the serial link - Im off to compusa today to see if I can get the card adapter for my laptop.||||reg||1
Z||000003||btoth||06-25-2001||10:22 AM||||I have the SanDisk USB card reader for my camera.  It's at least as fast as a ZIP drive.  Just drag and drop like any other disk drive... sure beats plugging in the camera and "uploading".||||reg||1
Z||000004||SteveJ||06-25-2001||11:17 AM||||Nice camera, especially for the price.<P>I have an older Panasonic and have had no problems with the<BR>serial connection but it's starting to flare colors now so I <BR>guess a new one is in order.<p>[This message has been edited by SteveJ (edited 06-25-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Ken Wittlief||06-25-2001||11:25 AM||||one thing you have to be carefull about with a digital camera or camcorder - if you accidentally point it at the sun when the lens is exposed it can destroy the CCD, just like holding a magnifying glass over a spider (hehehehehe)<P>  I noticed walking around with mine on a pier yesterday, that would be easy to do, esp with no lens cap.<P>edit: also I see those USB card readers on yahoo shopping - $28 to $48 dollars - transfer the whole card in 8 seconds instead of 60 minutes - I think I see one in my future (c%<p>[This message has been edited by Ken Wittlief (edited 06-25-2001).]||||reg||1
